# hardware run: stress build, PATTERN=1 VC_MODE=2, ECC_INJECT_DBE (bits 0 and 5 of every codeword flipped on write)
# board: Arty A7-100T (xc7a100t), Digilent 210319C088F2A
# date: 2026-09-12
# RTL: de8cac3 (bug #7 fix) — same sources as the clean run of the same day
# MARK_DEBUG 1104 nets -> 5 ILA cores / 55 probes / 1100 bits
#
# purpose: prove the double-bit alarm path on silicon (only the single-bit path had been run
# before, 2026-09-10). Expected and got: ecc_dbe_cnt=3, node_dbe=1111, sbe=0.
#
# Why sequence errors are 0 even though every word is corrupted: the injector flips
# codeword bit 5 = data bit d2 (hamming_word[5]) in every FIFO write, and a flit crosses
# exactly two async FIFOs (TX at the source, RX at the sink). Two deterministic flips of the
# same bit cancel, so the payload reaching the checker is correct while both FIFOs flag
# double_err. The alarm path is proved; end-to-end data corruption under an uncorrectable
# error is shown by tb_noc_stress_tester INJECT_ECC=1 (single-FIFO flip, 247 sequence
# errors), not by this build. verilog_define was cleared after this build.

